[list]
[*]New: a mod setting, [b]New stands are used for shift changes[/b], on by default. Turn it off and every outfit stand built from then on starts as "Not used for shift changes": ordinary furniture until you set it up with its switch. Stands that already exist keep their own setting, whichever way it is set. Requested by a player.
[*]New: hovering a stand's switch or its Set owner button now marks that stand on the map with the pulsing square vanilla shows on a target you are about to pick. An arrow points to it as well, as it does when you hover a storage link. With several stands selected, each stand shows its own pair of buttons, and until now nothing on them said which stand they belong to.
[*]Fixed: the description of [b]Unassigned stands are shared[/b] said that with it off, an unassigned stand behaves exactly like vanilla furniture. It does not: it dresses nobody, but "Allow removing items" stays off and its contents stay out of trade. The description now says so, and points at "Not used for shift changes" for a stand that should be ordinary furniture. How the setting works is unchanged.
[*]Fixed: if a stand's owner was kidnapped while the stand was boxed up for a move, setting it down made them its owner again and kept the shift they had open at it, so nobody else could use it until they came home. A kidnapped owner is now dropped when the stand is placed, as they already were from a stand left standing. In a save where a stand was already set down this way, loading the save releases the shift; the owner still needs removing once with Set owner.
[*]Fixed: on RimWorld 1.7, clicking the greyed Automatic option in a stand's settings, on a stand serving a radius or an allowed area, played a click though nothing changed. It is silent now.
[*]Unchanged: with the new setting left on, a new stand starts in service as before, and turning it off changes no stand you already have.
[/list]
